   "id": null,
   "title": "A vision redefined, a legacy renewed",
   "intro": "From her powerful full-displacement hull to the sleek lines that give her a timeless presence on the water, the Grand Trawler 63 balances grace and functionality. Developed in collaboration with MICAD Naval Architects, this yacht delivers remarkable fuel efficiency—offering up to 1,000 nautical miles of range at 9 knots with 10% fuel reserve.\nTrue comfort was a driving focus in her design and execution, and is successfully achieved in a number of ways – from the Sleipner fins which guarantee modern stabilization underway and at anchor, to the extensive soundproofing of her living quarters, to the studied comfort of her multiple seating areas – no aspect is ignored, no detail is overlooked.\nShe is also remarkable for the space she offers, both in terms of living area and in terms of storage capacity – an essential feature for those who seek long stretches of time on the water.",
