   "items": [
    {
     "title": "Exceptional Range and Fuel Efficiency",
     "text": "Thanks to her full-displacement hull developed with MICAD, the Grand Trawler 63 offers up to 1,000 nautical miles of range at 9 knots with a 10% fuel reserve—class-leading performance that expands your horizon.\nThe twin MAN engines with straight shafts deliver one of the best power-to-weight ratios on the market, no-nonsense reliability, and the finest manufacturer warranty available to owners today. What is the result? True peace of mind."
    },
    {
     "title": "Ultra-Quiet Cruising Experience",
     "text": "Because sound management is such an important part of cruising, the Grand Trawler 63 integrates Sleipner fin stabilizers, an optional Silent Boat Pack, and extensive soundproofing throughout.\nThe result is a whisper-quiet environment, both underway and at anchor, allowing your ears to focus on what matters – the sound of the ocean, the sound of laughter, the sound of music."
    },
    {
     "title": "Next-Generation Helm and Navigation",
     "text": "The newly redesigned helm station—drawing inspiration from the Swift Trawler 54—features floating MFD screens and a new Xenta electric steering system, offering a modern, responsive, and pleasant piloting experience.\nThe ergonomics are remarkably good – everything is where it should be – and the seating arrangements set a new standard of comfort, both in the captain’s chairs and the lovely daybed to port."
    }
   ],
